{"created": "2026-06-02T19:36:11.851482+00:00", "modified": "2026-06-07T13:59:34.122495+00:00", "id": 20515068, "conceptrecid": "20515067", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20515068", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.20515067", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20515068", "metadata": {"title": "Agulhas System Climate Array (ASCA) Twenty six month cross sectional gridded along track and cross track velocity, temperature, and salinity of the Agulhas Current", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20515068", "publication_date": "2026-06-02", "description": "<pre class=\"vC7TJ allowTextSelection\">Agulhas System Climate Array (ASCA) gridded temperature, salinity, and along track and cross track current velocity from April 2016 - June 2018. Derived from microCATs, current meters, ADCPs, and CPIES as detailed in references.</pre>\n<p>This dataset is 26 months of gridded cross sectional velocity, temperature, and salinity, from the Agulhas System Climate Array (ASCA). These velocities, temperatures, and salinities are used to create the volume, temperature, and salt transport time series (above).</p>\n<p>If you use these data, please include the following citation and acknowledgement:&nbsp;<br>Gridded cross-sectional velocities, temperatures, and salinities are based on in situ current meter measurements from the Agulhas System Climate Array (ASCA) experiment (McMonigal et al., 2020; Gunn et al., 2020)</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Beal, Lisa", "affiliation": "University of Miami", "orcid": "0000-0003-3678-5367"}], "contributors": [{"name": "McMonigal, K", "affiliation": "University of Alaska Fairbanks", "type": "DataCurator"}, {"name": "Gunn, Kathryn", "affiliation": "University of Southampton", "type": "DataCurator", "orcid": "0000-0003-2397-5364"}, {"name": "Novelli, Guillaume", "affiliation": "university of miami", "type": "DataManager", "orcid": "0000-0001-9560-7304"}], "keywords": ["Agulhas", "salinity", "temperature", "velocity", "indian ocean"], "references": [